==============================================================================================================================
E-6  GAUGE-INVARIANT CONTENT OF THE INTEGER LIFTS, AND THE QUANTISATION BOUND -- EXACT
==============================================================================================================================

(A)  MINIMUM OF EACH INTEGER LIFT OVER THE FULL STABILISER ORBIT OF THE PAIR (|S|^2 = 16 reps)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  n     pairs      exhaustive  pairs with sp_F2 = 0     of those, min I_unsigned > 0 min |I_signed| > 0         CTRL 1 / 0    
  4     105        YES         45                       0                        0                          1 / 0 OK      
  6     32385      YES         16065                    360                      0                          1 / 0 OK      
  8     19701      sampled     10546                    2255                     389                        1 / 0 OK      
  10    19701      sampled     12574                    2895                     113                        1 / 0 OK      
  12    21945      sampled     18135                    1664                     792                        1 / 0 OK      

  READ: 'min I_unsigned > 0' counts pairs whose integer intersection number CANNOT be gauged
        away.  A zero in that column means the integer lift's whole gauge-invariant content is
        its F_2 reduction, i.e. the intersection number carries nothing the pairing does not.

==============================================================================================================================
(B)  QUANTISATION.  Exhaustive over words and over integer-coefficient polynomials.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  n     words tested   values of Tr(Pi W)/Tr(Pi)      min NON-ZERO modulus^2 seen    any value with 0<|v|<1? 
  4     40000          {-6, -5, -4, -3, -2, -1, 0, +1, +2...} 1                              NO -- none exists       
  6     40000          {-5, -4, -3, -2, -1, 0, +1, +2, +3...} 1                              NO -- none exists       
  8     40000          {-6, -5, -4, -3, -2, -1, 0, +1, +2...} 1                              NO -- none exists       
  10    40000          {-5, -4, -3, -2, -1, 0, +1, +2, +3...} 1                              NO -- none exists       
  12    40000          {-6, -5, -4, -3, -2, -1, 0, +1, +2...} 1                              NO -- none exists       
  16    40000          {-6, -5, -4, -3, -2, -1, 0, +1, +2...} 1                              NO -- none exists       
  20    40000          {-5, -4, -3, -2, -1, 0, +1, +2, +3...} 1                              NO -- none exists       

  EXACT ARGUMENT, valid at every n and every word length: a product of Paulis is a single
  signed Pauli i^m W(c); Tr(Pi i^m W(c))/Tr(Pi) is 0 when c is not a stabiliser and a fourth
  root of unity when it is.  Linearity then puts every Gaussian-integer-coefficient polynomial
  scalar in Z[i].  Z[i] has NO element of modulus strictly between 0 and 1.
  no counterexample found in the sweep above: True

